The legal text is the Constitution of the Republic of Iraq, as published in the Official Gazette (Al-Waqa'i' Al-Iraqiya,
no. 4012, 28 December 2005).

The bytes here come from a third-party host: the College of Law, Al-Muthanna University (law.mu.edu.iq), page
"دستور جمهورية العراق لسنة 2005". Credit for the bytes: College of Law, Al-Muthanna University. The page states no terms
of use. The words were not changed; the text was only split into files and lines. It carries vowel marks that the Gazette
prints only in part; they are kept as the host prints them. The text was checked against the Gazette scan hosted by WIPO
Lex (https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/ar/legislation/details/10027).

Why it may be published: Iraq Copyright Law no. 3 of 1971, Article 6(3) ("المادة السادسة") says that protection does not
extend to:

  "مجموعات الوثائق الرسمية كنصوص القوانين والأنظمة والاتفاقات الدولية والأحكام القضائية وسائر الوثائق الرسمية"
  (collections of official documents such as the texts of laws, regulations, international agreements, judicial decisions
  and other official documents),

with the proviso that such a collection is protected where it is distinguished by originality, arrangement or other
personal effort. The text here follows the Gazette; it adds no selection or arrangement of its own beyond one file per
article. Source for the Act: https://ar.wikisource.org/ (Law no. 3 of 1971).

